        "title": {
          "en": "A busy day"
        },
        "text": {
          "en": "Anu said, \"I read daily. I am reading now. I have read this book twice.\"\n\"Each sentence shows a different time and stage,\" said the teacher."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "explain",
        "type": "explanation",
        "provenance": "original",
        "keepEnglishTerms": [
          "simple",
          "continuous",
          "perfect"
        ],
        "text": {
          "en": "Simple present: she plays. Simple past: she played. Simple future: she will play.\nPresent continuous shows an action going on now: she is playing. Past continuous: she was playing. It uses is, am, are or was, were with the ing form.\nPresent perfect shows a finished action linked to now: she has played. It uses has or have with the past participle."
        }
      },
